{"name":"Silver Fox","hex":"#bdbcc4","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"silver fox","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A melanistic red fox (Vulpes vulpes) with silver to black fur.","A domestic rabbit of a rare breed with silvery-black fur."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/silver_fox"}],"entries":[{"title":"Silver fox (animal)","blocks":[{"text":"The silver fox, sometimes referred to as the black fox, or blue fox, is a melanistic form of the red fox. Silver foxes display a great deal of pelt variation. Some are completely glossy black except for a white colouration on the tip of the tail, giving them a somewhat silvery appearance. Some silver foxes are bluish-grey, and some may have a cinereous colour on the sides."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a7/Silberfuchs_08.jpg/330px-Silberfuchs_08.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Silver_fox_(animal)"},{"title":"Edith Somerville","blocks":[{"text":"Edith Anna Œnone Somerville was an Irish novelist who habitually signed herself as \"E. Œ. Somerville\". She wrote in collaboration with her cousin \"Martin Ross\" under the pseudonym \"Somerville and Ross\". Together they published a series of fourteen stories and novels, the most popular of which were The Real Charlotte, published in 1894, and Some Experiences of an Irish R. M., published in 1899."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/36/Irish_memories_%281919%29_%2814576433540%29.jpg/330px-Irish_memories_%281919%29_%2814576433540%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Edith_Somerville"},{"title":"Fox","blocks":[{"text":"Foxes are small-to-medium-sized omnivorous mammals belonging to several genera of the family Canidae. They have a flattened skull; upright, triangular ears; a pointed, slightly upturned snout; and a long, bushy tail (\"brush\")."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/30/Vulpes_vulpes_ssp_fulvus.jpg/330px-Vulpes_vulpes_ssp_fulvus.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fox"},{"title":"Silver","blocks":[{"text":"Silver is a chemical element; it has symbol Ag and atomic number 47. A soft, white, lustrous transition metal, it exhibits the highest electrical conductivity, thermal conductivity and reflectivity of any metal. Silver is found in the Earth's crust in the pure, free elemental form, as an alloy with gold (electrum) and other metals, and in minerals such as acanthite, argentite and chlorargyrite. Most silver is recovered as a byproduct of lead–zinc, copper and gold mining and refining."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/55/Silver_crystal.jpg/330px-Silver_crystal.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Silver"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2c/Silberfuchs_06.jpg/500px-Silberfuchs_06.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2c/Silberfuchs_06.jpg/1280px-Silberfuchs_06.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2c/Silberfuchs_06.jpg/500px-Silberfuchs_06.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"An adult silver fox","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASilberfuchs_06.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c9/Fur_silverfox.jpg/330px-Fur_silverfox.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c9/Fur_silverfox.jpg/330px-Fur_silverfox.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Silver fox furs","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AFur_silverfox.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fd/Feeding_the_silver_foxes_%28c_1901%29.jpg/500px-Feeding_the_silver_foxes_%28c_1901%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fd/Feeding_the_silver_foxes_%28c_1901%29.jpg/1280px-Feeding_the_silver_foxes_%28c_1901%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fd/Feeding_the_silver_foxes_%28c_1901%29.jpg/500px-Feeding_the_silver_foxes_%28c_1901%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Captive silver foxes being fed","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AFeeding_the_silver_foxes_(c_1901).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b6/All_on_the_Irish_shore_-_Irish_sketches_%281910%29_%2814776964144%29.jpg/500px-All_on_the_Irish_shore_-_Irish_sketches_%281910%29_%2814776964144%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b6/All_on_the_Irish_shore_-_Irish_sketches_%281910%29_%2814776964144%29.jpg/1280px-All_on_the_Irish_shore_-_Irish_sketches_%281910%29_%2814776964144%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b6/All_on_the_Irish_shore_-_Irish_sketches_%281910%29_%2814776964144%29.jpg/500px-All_on_the_Irish_shore_-_Irish_sketches_%281910%29_%2814776964144%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"An illustration by Somerville in All on the Irish Shore","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AAll_on_the_Irish_shore_-_Irish_sketches_(1910)_(14776964144).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.